Alerts on suspicious trading, regulatory reports.

59
00:04:29.155 --> 00:04:31.309
Scale for this design (assumptions).

60
00:04:31.589 --> 00:04:32.933
Here is a quick table:

61
00:04:33.213 --> 00:04:34.536
Quantity, and Value.

62
00:04:34.816 --> 00:04:35.989
Active clients:

63
00:04:36.269 --> 00:04:39.363
10M; 1.5M trading on a busy day.

64
00:04:39.643 --> 00:04:40.731
Orders per day:

65
00:04:41.011 --> 00:04:43.763
10 to 20M (F and O-heavy days higher).

66
00:04:44.043 --> 00:04:52.192
Peak order rate: ~20 to 50k orders per second in the first minute after 9:15 am and on volatile events.

67
00:04:52.472 --> 00:04:59.064
Instruments: ~100k tradable (equities, derivatives contracts across expiries and strikes).

68
00:04:59.344 --> 00:05:00.965
Market data ticks received:

69
00:05:01.245 --> 00:05:04.403
Hundreds of thousands per second at peak across segments.

70
00:05:04.683 --> 00:05:06.432
Concurrent WebSocket clients:

71
00:05:06.712 --> 00:05:08.675
2 to 3M at market open.

72
00:05:08.955 --> 00:05:10.917
Subscribed instruments per client:

73
00:05:11.197 --> 00:05:14.525
10 to 200 (watchlists, positions, option chains).

74
00:05:15.875 --> 00:05:18.585
Estimation, the ticker is the biggest fan-out:

75
00:05:18.865 --> 00:05:23.686
Sending every tick of every subscribed instrument to every client is impossible:

76
00:05:23.966 --> 00:05:31.518
3M clients times 50 instruments times several ticks per second is hundreds of millions of messages per second.

77
00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:43.745
So the ticker conflates: it sends each client at most one update per instrument per interval (for example, 1 s or 250 ms) with the latest values (§6.4).

78
00:05:44.025 --> 00:05:49.806
Even then it is tens of millions of messages per second across a fleet of WebSocket servers.

79
00:05:50.086 --> 00:05:53.691
That is why market data uses compact binary formats.

80
00:05:55.041 --> 00:05:55.916
Part 2.

81
00:05:56.196 --> 00:05:57.156
Requirements.

82
00:05:58.406 --> 00:05:59.259
Functional.

83
00:05:59.539 --> 00:06:00.990
Open an account online:

84
00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:12.193
KYC, PAN verification, bank account verification, e-sign, demat account, nominee, segment activation (F and O needs income proof per rules; VERIFY).

85
00:06:12.473 --> 00:06:17.614
Add funds instantly (UPI or net banking), withdraw to the linked bank, see the ledger.

86
00:06:17.894 --> 00:06:24.870
Watchlists with live prices; market depth (5 levels or more); option chains; charts with historical data.

87
00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:44.183
Place orders: market, limit, stop-loss, stop-loss market; product types (delivery or CNC, intraday or MIS, normal or NRML for F and O); after-market orders (AMO); basket orders; iceberg orders; GTT (good till triggered); modify and cancel.

88
00:06:44.463 --> 00:06:50.927
See orders, trades, positions (intraday and overnight), holdings, P and L, margin used and available.

89
00:06:51.207 --> 00:06:53.468
Pledge holdings for margin (collateral).

90
00:06:53.748 --> 00:06:57.908
Mutual fund purchases and SIPs; IPO applications.

91
00:06:59.258 --> 00:07:05.871
Contract notes, ledgers, tax P and L reports, and corporate action handling (dividends, splits, bonuses).

92
00:07:06.151 --> 00:07:13.639
APIs for programmatic trading, with rate limits and algo rules (VERIFY SEBI's framework for retail algo trading).

93
00:07:14.989 --> 00:07:16.099
Non-functional.

94
00:07:16.379 --> 00:07:17.723
Here is a quick table:

95
00:07:18.003 --> 00:07:19.368
Attribute, and Target.

96
00:07:19.648 --> 00:07:20.736
Order latency:

97
00:07:21.016 --> 00:07:29.421
Client tap to exchange ack in tens of ms (network-dominated); broker's internal processing a few ms p99.

98
00:07:29.701 --> 00:07:30.619
Correctness:

99
00:07:30.899 --> 00:07:36.253
No order accepted without margin; no double-sending; positions and funds exact.

100
00:07:36.533 --> 00:07:37.600
Availability:

101
00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:49.315
During market hours ≥ 99.99%; any outage during market hours is highly visible and may need to be reported to exchanges (VERIFY).

102
00:07:49.595 --> 00:07:50.597
Market data:

103
00:07:50.877 --> 00:07:55.293
Tick-to-screen within ~1 s for retail; depth updates consistent.

104
00:07:55.573 --> 00:07:56.320
Scale:

105
00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:00.376
Market open spike (orders, logins, WebSocket connects).

106
00:08:00.656 --> 00:08:01.637
Auditability:

107
00:08:01.917 --> 00:08:09.128
Every order, modification and risk decision logged with timestamps; records retained per regulation (VERIFY).

108
00:08:10.478 --> 00:08:11.481
Security:

109
